# MySQL Extractor

Component ID: `keboola.ex-db-mysql`

## Overview

The MySQL Extractor allows you to extract data from MySQL databases.

## Configuration

### Connection

```json
{
  "parameters": {
    "db": {
      "host": "mysql.example.com",
      "port": 3306,
      "database": "production",
      "#user": "username",
      "#password": "password"
    }
  }
}
```

### Tables

```json
{
  "parameters": {
    "tables": [
      {
        "name": "customers",
        "outputTable": "in.c-mysql.customers",
        "incremental": true,
        "incrementalFetchingColumn": "updated_at",
        "primaryKey": ["id"]
      }
    ]
  }
}
```

## Best Practices

1. Always use incremental loading for large tables
2. Set appropriate primary keys
3. Use read-only database user
4. Enable SSL connections when possible
